{
  "requirement": "The SDK formats node inputs using `Contents::format_node_content`,\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.fingerprint_content`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Method on Contents. Both arguments describe the already-read snapshot.\n/// Present these supplied contents as text for an agent.\nfn format_node_content(\n    &self,\n    node: &Self::NodeId,\n    contents: &Self::NodeContent,\n) -> Result<String, Self::Error>;\n```\n\nThe formatter uses the supplied contents; their fingerprint describes the same\nread. For inputs queued on an ask builder, formatting errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node` tool call, a formatting error is\nreturned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue and recover.\n`NodeContent` and `NodeId` retain their application-defined types without\nserialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `judge.rendering`.\n\n- **Queued inputs are formatted with `format_node_content`.**\n  - `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` replaces the formatter with `distinct_pages` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs`. The `ParallelConversations` provider asserts that each conversation's first-turn history contains its own formatted marker (`ALPHA-CONTENTS` or `BETA-CONTENTS`) and never the other's. A bypass of the formatter would therefore fail.\n  - This relies on `Question` queueing node contents. I did not read its definition.\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` and `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` check that rendered inputs reach the agent in order. The second also checks the real `HabeasDomain`.\n- **The formatter uses the supplied contents, and the fingerprint describes the same read.**\n  - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` in `tests/contracts.rs` changes the underlying content after the read. It then asserts that `format_node_content` on the snapshot still returns \"before\", that the fingerprint is unchanged, and that only one read happened.\n  - `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` in `src/sdk.rs` formats supplied contents for a node whose file does not exist. It checks the output contains the supplied text and that a mismatched node kind gives an error.\n  - `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` checks that authoring keeps the prepared snapshot and fingerprint.\n- **Formatting errors on queued inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n  - `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` sets `fail_format`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`, no recorded dependencies, and no new agent requests.\n  - It also covers read failures and edge failures.\n- **A formatting error during `read_node` is returned to the agent as a tool error.**\n  - `node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` has the formatter fail. It asserts that the second request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, name `read_node` and the error text.\n  - The same test asserts that the agent then submits and `ask` succeeds, and that no dependency is recorded for the undelivered contents.\n  - The success path of `read_node` through the formatter is exercised in the `ParallelConversations` flow, where the `read_node` and `get_node_page` results contain the formatted markers.\n- **`NodeContent` and `NodeId` keep application-defined types without serialization or display bounds.** The `Node` type in `tests/agent.rs` deliberately has no Serde, Hash or Display. `Content` is also a bare struct. Because these types compile and are used through the full flow, the test suite exercises this constraint.\n\nI found no scenario that a requirement-violating implementation could pass undetected. Nothing is acknowledged by a `{fixme}`, and none is needed.",
  "references": "be8dfa22dce3f9297803609deae03b7b9d0aafd2150eb790d6da62f8e199b8aa",
